---
description: >-
  Label syntax (#1368, #1403): each section and leaf label written as plain markdown markers, a
  quoted markdown string, a code span in plain text, tags and a written `\n`; the title with
  plain markers, a tag break and a subscript. Only a quoted markdown string is markdown; tags draw and `\n` breaks. A
  section header is one line high, so it keeps a label's first line with `...` after it. Names
  are always quoted, so they have no bare-backtick form.
---
treemap-beta
  title title **bold** _ital_<br>next H<sub>2</sub>O
  "section **bold** _ital_"
    "leaf **bold** _ital_": 10
  "`section **bold** _ital_`"
    "`leaf **bold** _ital_`": 10
  "section a `code` b"
    "leaf a `code` b": 10
  "section <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O"
    "leaf <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O": 10
  "section one\ntwo"
    "leaf one\ntwo": 10
